You can create a class for each dialogue, each with a prompt and a list of options. Each option would have a description and a reference to the next dialogue. Then, you can have a loop that shows the current dialogue, gets the user input, and moves to the next dialogue.
For example, you could have a Dialogue class:
public class Dialogue {
    private String prompt;
    private List<Choice> choices;

    public Dialogue(String prompt, List<Choice> choices) {
        this.prompt = prompt;
        this.choices = choices;
    }

    public void display() {
        System.out.println(prompt);
        for (int i = 0; i < choices.size(); i++) {
            System.out.println((i + 1) + ". " + choices.get(i).getDescription());
        }
    }

    public Dialogue getChoice(int index) {
        return choices.get(index).getNextDialogue();
    }
}

public class Choice {
    private String description;
    private Dialogue nextDialogue;

    public Choice(String description, Dialogue nextDialogue) {
        this.description = description;
        this.nextDialogue = nextDialogue;
    }

    public String getDescription() {
        return description;
    }

    public Dialogue getNextDialogue() {
        return nextDialogue;
    }
}
